{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Experiment agreements — ",
    {{ project_id | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Generated by command `llmexer analysis add-agreement`.\n",
    "\n",
    "| | |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| project | `",
    {{ project_id | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "| llmexer version | `",
    {{ package_version | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "| generated | `",
    {{ generated_at | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "\n",
    "Cohen's kappa between every pair of configurations, for each yes/no field of\n",
    "the answers, within each prompt. Kappa discounts the agreement chance alone\n",
    "would produce, so it is the number to report rather than a raw match rate.\n",
    "\n",
    "`prompt_id` is the set each pair is scored within and `data_id` is the item\n",
    "they have to share to be compared, so one prompt's disagreement is never\n",
    "averaged away into another's.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook loads and flattens the experiment itself, so it runs on its own.\n",
    "The logic lives in `transform.py` and `agreement.py` next to it. Feel free to\n",
    "change the notebook for your needs and data.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Folders and input\n",
    "\n",
    "| variable | meaning |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `DIR_EXPERIMENT` | `<project>/experiment` |\n",
    "| `DB_FILE` | the database to analyse |\n",
    "| `CSV_FILE` | flattened answers, used only when there is no database |\n",
    "| `FIELDS` | yes/no fields to compare; empty means detect them |\n",
    "| `AUTODETECT_FIELDS` | find the yes/no fields when `FIELDS` is empty |\n",
    "| `INTERMEDIATE_VALUES_DIR` | folder for the per-item CSVs; `None` writes none |\n",
    "\n",
    "`DB_FILE` points at the newest `experiment_*.db` when this notebook was\n",
    "created, **no updates** after creation — change it by hand and re-run the cell.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# mapping experiment and analysis folders\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "ANALYSIS_DIR = Path.cwd()\n",
    "PROJECT_DIR = ANALYSIS_DIR.parent\n",
    "\n",
    "DIR_EXPERIMENT = PROJECT_DIR / 'experiment'\n",
    "PROJECT_ID = ",
    {{ project_id | tojson | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "# `transform` and `agreement` are the copies sitting next to this notebook\n",
    "if str(ANALYSIS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(ANALYSIS_DIR))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# imports of pre-designed methods/functions for analysis\n",
    "%load_ext autoreload\n",
    "%autoreload 2\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from agreement import kappa_matrix, pairwise_cohen_kappa, yes_no_fields\n",
    "from transform import (\n",
    "    flatten_llm_response,\n",
    "    flattened_only,\n",
    "    load_experiment_db,\n",
    "    load_flattened_csv,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.max_colwidth', 120)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- the only cell to edit ---\n",
    "DB_FILE = ",
    {{ db_file | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "CSV_FILE = ",
    {{ csv_file | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "FIELDS = ",
    {{ fields | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "AUTODETECT_FIELDS = ",
    {{ autodetect_fields | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set to a folder to also write the rows behind every kappa, one CSV per\n",
    "# prompt and pair, for checking a suspicious number by hand. None writes none.\n",
    "INTERMEDIATE_VALUES_DIR = None  # e.g. ANALYSIS_DIR / 'kappa_values'\n",
    "\n",
    "DB_PATH = DIR_EXPERIMENT / DB_FILE if DB_FILE else None\n",
    "CSV_PATH = ANALYSIS_DIR / CSV_FILE if CSV_FILE else None\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'project   : {PROJECT_ID}')\n",
    "print(f'database  : {DB_PATH}')\n",
    "print(f'fields    : {FIELDS}')\n",
    "print(f'autodetect: {AUTODETECT_FIELDS}')\n",
    "print(f'values dir: {INTERMEDIATE_VALUES_DIR}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load the experiment\n",
    "\n",
    "The newest `experiment_*.db` is used; set `DB_PATH` by hand to pick another.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = load_experiment_db(DB_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'database : {DB_PATH}')\n",
    "print(f'rows     : {len(df)}')\n",
    "df.head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Flatten the LLM model answers\n",
    "\n",
    "Each `response_text` is parsed as JSON and expanded into columns. Malformed\n",
    "answers keep their row and are reported in `flatten_error`; `experiment fix`\n",
    "repairs the ones that carry JSON next to prose.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_flat = flatten_llm_response(df)\n",
    "\n",
    "_bad = df_flat['flatten_error'].ne('')\n",
    "print(f'rows            : {len(df_flat)}')\n",
    "print(f'unparsed answers: {int(_bad.sum())}')\n",
    "df_flat.loc[_bad, ['code', 'flatten_error']].head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The answers to compare\n",
    "\n",
    "One row per combination: `code`, `data_id`, `prompt_id`, `model_name`,\n",
    "`provider_name`, `profile_name`\n",
    "and one column per key the models answered with — the same frame\n",
    "`analyse_experiment.ipynb` exports as `*_flattened.csv`.\n",
    "\n",
    "With no database to read, that exported CSV is used instead. Delete whichever\n",
    "branch you do not want.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "answers = flattened_only(df_flat)\n",
    "\n",
    "if answers.empty:\n",
    "    answers = load_flattened_csv(CSV_PATH)\n",
    "    print(f'read from: {CSV_PATH}')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f'read from: {DB_PATH}')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'rows: {len(answers)}')\n",
    "answers.head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Which fields are compared\n",
    "\n",
    "`FIELDS` wins when you set it. Otherwise every column whose values are all\n",
    "yes/no, true/false, y/n or 1/0 is picked up.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fields = list(FIELDS) if FIELDS else (yes_no_fields(answers) if AUTODETECT_FIELDS else [])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'comparing: {fields}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Filter the auto-detected fields if needed\n",
    "fields_to_remove = []\n",
    "fields = [x for x in fields if x not in fields_to_remove]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'comparing: {fields}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Working with `Cohens Kappa`\n",
    "\n",
    "`cohen_kappa` is computed with\n",
    "[`sklearn.metrics.cohen_kappa_score`](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.cohen_kappa_score.html).\n",
    "\n",
    "<details>\n",
    "<summary>Paper from Landis & Koch</summary>\n",
    "\n",
    "Landis, J. R. and Koch, G. G. (1977). The measurement of observer agreement for\n",
    "categorical data. *Biometrics*, 33(1), 159-174.\n",
    "[doi:10.2307/2529310](https://doi.org/10.2307/2529310)\n",
    "\n",
    "</details>\n",
    "\n",
    "Landis & Koch read kappa as:\n",
    "\n",
    "| kappa | agreement |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `< 0.00` | poor |\n",
    "| `0.00 - 0.20` | slight |\n",
    "| `0.21 - 0.40` | fair |\n",
    "| `0.41 - 0.60` | moderate |\n",
    "| `0.61 - 0.80` | substantial |\n",
    "| `0.81 - 1.00` | almost perfect |\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "### Further usage examples\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# the pairs that agree least, whatever the field\n",
    "kappa.sort_values('cohen_kappa').head(10)\n",
    "\n",
    "# one field as a configuration x configuration matrix\n",
    "kappa_matrix(kappa, fields[0], kappa['prompt_id'].iloc[0])\n",
    "\n",
    "# average agreement per field\n",
    "kappa.groupby(['prompt_id', 'field'])['cohen_kappa'].mean().sort_values()\n",
    "\n",
    "# only the pairs that share the same model, i.e. profile against profile\n",
    "kappa[kappa['model_a'] == kappa['model_b']]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Run calculations for Cohens kappa\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "kappa = pairwise_cohen_kappa(answers, fields, intermediate_values_dir=INTERMEDIATE_VALUES_DIR)\n",
    "\n",
    "kappa\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
